# local env files
#
# Deliberately a WILDCARD with one exception, not a list of known names. The list
# form covered .env and .env.*.local but NOT .env.bak.<timestamp>, which is what
# scripts/sync-env.sh writes before it edits an env file. Those backups are full
# copies including credentials, they sat in the tree unignored, and a `git add -A`
# would have committed them. Any future .env variant is now covered by default.
.env*
!.env.example

